(6263800, 925915, 53094, '<td valign="top">Deb, this is a great photo!  Our cats have never met a bag or box they didn''t like.  The detail in Thomas'' eyes are just incredible.  Congratulations on your well deserved ribbon.</td>', 'Deb, this is a great photo!  Our cats have never met a bag or box they didn''t like.  The detail in Thomas'' eyes are just incredible.  Congratulations on your well deserved ribbon.', '2010-12-29 12:55:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(6263808, 925871, 54446, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Yo_Spiff:</b></div><hr/><i> Why are these cats always named Bob? Aren''t there any Frankcats or Davidcats? How about a Josecat? </i></td></tr></table> <br/>It''s a good question, which has a rational answer.  Bobcats are named that because of their "bobbed" tail.<br/> <br/>We have mountain lions in the area, too.  They are dramatic by contrast because of their very long tail, almost as long again as their body.</td>', 'Originally posted by Yo_Spiff: Why are these cats always named Bob? Aren''t there any Frankcats or Davidcats? How about a Josecat?  It''s a good question, which has a rational answer.  Bobcats are named that because of their "bobbed" tail. We have mountain lions in the area, too.  They are dramatic by contrast because of their very long tail, almost as long again as their body.', '2010-12-29 13:00:13.000000', NULL, 0),
